Development checkpoint only; no blanket redistribution license is asserted.

Upstream kawin material retains its MIT notice, reproduced verbatim in NOTICE.
Public kawin services remain dependency-owned.

MAP-origin material is subject to the Materials Algorithms Project's published
redistribution conditions, summarized with attribution and source links in NOTICE:
credit MAP and the originators in documentation and source, identify modifications,
and do not charge for subsequent distribution. These conditions are distinct from
the upstream MIT terms; MAP-origin material is not offered under a blanket MIT grant.

Local Illingworth solver, numerical/mesh and provider modules, plus bounded
host-policy methods, are copied/adapted from the research fork. Recording MAP's
permission does not determine ownership or grant a license for separately authored
local additions. Their ownership and a package-wide license remain separate release
decisions; this file makes no new grant covering the whole fork.
